# Copy this file as model.txt to choose your LLM (lines starting with # are ignored; the first valid line is used).
#   cp model.txt.example model.txt
# Enter a model name supported by your API endpoint/gateway.
# It is highly recommended to select a model that supports function calling (tools),
# otherwise ZetaJarvis's abilities to open apps, read screens, save memory, etc., will fail. Common choices:
#   openrouter/free
#   deepseek-chat       (DeepSeek V3, supports tools, highly cost-effective)
#   gpt-4o / gpt-4o-mini
#   claude-3-5-sonnet   (If your gateway/endpoint forwards to Claude)
# The environment variable JARVIS_MODEL has higher priority.
openrouter/free
